---
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import characterx from "../images/characterx.png";
import charactery from "../images/charactery.png";
import canonrules from "../images/canonrules.gif";
---

<article>
  <details>
    <summary>Can I make fanworks with your characters?</summary>

    <p>
      Yes, <em>please</em>. Fanfic, fanart, memes, meta, elaborate shipping
      charts... literally anything (and we really do mean <em>anything</em>)
      your fannish heart desires!
    </p>
    <p>
      We're making these characters for fandom, and thus, <strong>you</strong> to
      play with. Consider them your dolls, so go ahead and give your faves a happy
      ending, put them through the wringer, and smash them together however you please.
    </p>
    <p>We're excited to see what you make!</p>
  </details>
</article>

<article>
  <details>
    <summary>How much room is there for headcanons?</summary>

    <p>
      <em>All</em> the room. Our designs and character profiles are just a starting
      point, not canon <em>per se</em>. They're not meant to limit your
      imagination, but to spark your interest instead.
    </p>
    <figure class="gif">
      <img
        src={canonrules.src}
        width={canonrules.width}
        height={canonrules.height}
        alt="GIF of Captain Barbossa from Pirates of the Caribbean saying 'The canon is more what you'd call guidelines than actual rules.'"
      />
    </figure>
    <p>
      We welcome your takes on our characters' backgrounds, personalities,
      genders, pronouns, relationships; all of it. We can only hope these
      characters stick with you long enough to inspire you that way.
    </p>
    <p>
      For our part, we use he/him for the programming gijinka in official
      materials as a nod to the genres that inspired FujoGuide. That's our
      convention, it doesn't need to be yours!
    </p>
  </details>
</article>

<article>
  <details>
    <summary>What goes into designing the cast?</summary>

    <p>
      We bring the characters to life by combining programming concepts and our
      favorite character tropes. We decide how characters fit together and
      develop their looks, personalities and quirks to make them feel unique and
      memorable.
    </p>
    <p>
      The research stage involves pulling bits from our own experiences and
      those around us and, of course, going down plenty of rabbit holes. When we
      need a perspective we don't have, we bring in outside consultants. For
      CSS, that meant working with <a href="/contributors/moon">Moon</a>, our
      Mi'kmaq sensitivity reader, and a deaf sensitivity reader who prefers to
      remain anonymous. You can see all our collaborators on our
      <a href="/contributors">contributors page</a>.
    </p>
  </details>
</article>

<article>
  <details>
    <summary>Are there more characters upcoming?</summary>

    <p>
      Oh, so many. We started developing the cast before we'd settled on what
      Volume 0 would cover, which means we built out a lot of characters who
      haven't had their turn in the spotlight yet.
    </p>
    <p>Here's a little sneak peek:</p>
    <figure>
      <Image
        src={characterx}
        alt="Sketches of the unreleased FujoGuide character [Redacted]. He has a thicc build, a medium-dark skin tone, and tightly curled black hair shown in different styles. On the left is a nearly full-body drawing of him wearing a patchwork sweater, smiling, with a flat top hair style, and holding a steaming mug. The artist's notes read 'dimples? uwu'. In the middle are two side profiles with hair ideas: the top one has a flat top with fade hair style and the bottom one has box braids on top with a fade. The artist's notes read 'yarn braids :3'. On the right is a drawing of him knitting with his elbows on the table and his tongue sticking out in focus mode. He is wearing a white long-sleeve shirt and a very short hairstyle. The artist's notes read 'focusing too hard'."
      />
      <Image
        src={charactery}
        alt="Sketches of the unreleased FujoGuide character [Redacted]. He has a thin build, a light skin tone, and long hair swept to one side and gathered in a ponytail. He is neatly dressed in a button down shirt, collared vest, dress pants, driving gloves, and oval bottom rim glasses. On the left, he is holding and reading a large book. In the middle, he is sitting cross-legged and looking thoughtful with a finger on his lips. On the right, he is walking down a grand staircase with one hand on the railing and a pencil behind his ear."
      />
    </figure>
    <p>
      We can't go into many details because they will be featured in future
      volumes, but know that there are so, so many more hot anime boys waiting
      for you.
    </p>
  </details>
</article>

<style>
  article {
    background-color: white;
    padding: 25px 30px;
    border-radius: 10px;
    row-gap: 10px;
    box-shadow: 2px 2px 0px 0px var(--text-color-disabled);
    margin: 0 auto;
    width: 100%;
    border: 2px dashed var(--terminal-dark);
  }

  summary {
    font-family: "freude", sans-serif;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--fujo-red);
    font-size: larger;
  }

  p,
  ul {
    line-height: 1.8;
    padding-inline: 10px;
  }
  ul {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    padding-left: 1rem;
  }

  li {
    margin-left: 20px;
  }

  figure {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    margin-top: 10px;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }

  img {
    min-width: 300px;
    max-width: 50%;
    height: auto;
  }

  figure.gif {
    margin-inline: 0;
  }

  figure.gif img {
    max-width: 80%;
  }

  @media (max-width: 749px) {
    article {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      align-content: center;
      align-items: center;
      max-width: 90vw;
      padding: 18px 20px;
    }

    figure {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      margin-top: 10px;
      margin-bottom: 10px;
    }
  }
</style>
